    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Heartforge of the Great Work.</strong> You have become less of a person and more of a walking repair script for reality.</p><ul><li>Once per <strong>strategic turn</strong>, when your faction undertakes a major operation centered on <strong>repair, healing, cleansing, or reconstruction</strong> (hex restoration, rebuilding a bastion, reclaiming a corrupted site, mending a shattered community), you may invoke this feature.</li><li>The operation automatically <strong>avoids catastrophic failure</strong>. A failure becomes a partial success; a partial success becomes a full success; or a full success gains an additional <strong>restorative rider</strong> (such as an extra point of Darkness reduction, Loyalty gain, or hex status improvement), at the GM’s discretion.</li><li>On the world scale, your presence gradually leaves regions you work in with a baseline bias toward <strong>stability and healing</strong>. People start saying things like, “If the Soul-Smith sets up shop here, this place is going to make it.”</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
